<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>FIR Complaint Letter — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Section 173 Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS) 2023 / Section 154 Code of Criminal Procedure 1973</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>No court fee or stamp duty required (Statutory right to lodge complaint for cognizable offence)</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>To be lodged directly at the jurisdictional Police Station having territorial jurisdiction</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Not required; Self-signed complaint submitted in duplicate with acknowledgment seal</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Jurisdictional Judicial Magistrate First Class (JMFC) having supervision over police station</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>Immediate reporting recommended; Delay must be explained reasonably in the complaint narrative</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Government Photo Identity Proof of Complainant; Photographs / CCTV footage / Call audio records / Bank transaction statements (if applicable); Medical Examination Report (MLC) in case of physical assault</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">FIR COMPLAINT LETTER</div>
<div class="draft-body">COMPLAINT UNDER SECTION 173 BNSS 2023 / SECTION 154 CRPC FOR REGISTRATION OF FIR

Date: ___/___/2026
To,
The Station House Officer (SHO),
________________________________ Police Station,
District / City: ________________________, Karnataka.

SUBJECT: WRITTEN COMPLAINT REGARDING COMMISSION OF COGNIZABLE OFFENCE OF ____________________________________ (THEFT / CHEATING / ASSAULT / CRIMINAL INTIMIDATION) AT ________________________ ON ___/___/2026.

Respected Sir/Madam,

I, the undersigned Complainant, __________________________________________________, S/o, D/o __________________________________________________, aged _____ years, residing at ______________________________________________________________________, Mobile No.: ________________________, Aadhaar No.: ________________________, respectfully lodge this complaint as follows:

1. TIME & PLACE OF INCIDENT:
The incident occurred on ___/___/2026 at approximately ____:____ AM/PM at ______________________________________________________________________.

2. DETAILS OF ACCUSED PERSON(S):
Name(s): ____________________________________________________________________
Address / Identification: ____________________________________________________
(Or unknown persons described as: ___________________________________________)

3. DETAILED STATEMENT OF FACTS:
(a) That on the date and time mentioned above, while I was ________________________________________, the accused person(s) unlawfully ____________________________________________________________________
(b) That the accused committed the following acts: ___________________________________________________
(c) That as a result of the said illegal acts, I suffered loss/injury of Rs. ____________ / physical hurt.

4. EVIDENCE ENCLOSED:
(i) Copy of Photo ID; (ii) Bank Statement / Transaction ID; (iii) CCTV Stills / Photographs; (iv) Medical certificate.

PRAYER:
In view of the above facts, I earnestly request your good office to register a First Information Report (FIR) under the appropriate provisions of Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) 2023 / Indian Penal Code against the accused person(s), initiate prompt investigation, and provide me with an acknowledgment / free copy of the FIR as mandated by law.

Yours faithfully,

___________________________________________
COMPLAINANT SIGNATURE
Name: _____________________________________
Mobile: ___________________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>